  "facts": [
    "The Sunniberg Bridge, finished in 1998, stretches 526 m with a 500 m horizontal radius, soaring 50–60 m above the Landquart valley and showcasing Christian Menn’s elegant extradosed design.",
    "Constructed by Batigroup AG and Vetsch AG, the bridge’s balanced cantilever deck was erected after four slender H‑shaped piers rose from the valley floor, each flaring like alpine trees.",
    "Awarded the 2001 Outstanding Structure Award, the bridge earned acclaim for marrying economic efficiency with artistic form, cementing extradosed bridges as a distinct, celebrated type."
